<title>UK: IGC lowers China wheat import estimate to 7.0 mln.</title>
<headline>IGC lowers China wheat import estimate to 7.0 mln.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Grains Council (IGC) on Tuesday reduced its estimate for Chinese wheat imports by one million tonnes to seven million tonnes in the current 1996/97 (July/June) season.</p>
<p>But the change was offset by small upward revisions in other countries and the IGC in its latest monthly report kept its world wheat trade estimate at a steady 89 million tonnes.</p>
<p>This compares with 90 million tonnes in 1995/96.</p>
<p>The reduction in China's imports followed an increase in the estimate for the country's 1996 wheat crop of one million tonnes to 108 million tonnes following better yields.</p>
<p>China's coarse grain output estimate was also revised up to a substantial 128 million tonnes from 124 million last month.</p>
<p>-- Clelia Oziel, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8072</p>
